🔹 5. Hooks
📍 Location: hooks/
📌 Purpose: Provides setup and teardown logic for tests (e.g., starting the browser,
 closing it, taking screenshots on failure).
🔗 Connected to: Step Definitions (stepDefinitions/), DriverFactory (factory/)

📌 Example: (from MyHooks.java)

java
Copy
Edit
@Before
public void setUp() {
    driver = DriverFactory.getDriver();
}

@After
public void tearDown() {
    driver.quit();
}
➡ Ensures browser is initialized and closed properly.

🔹 6. Driver Factory
📍 Location: factory/
📌 Purpose: Manages WebDriver instances, allowing flexible browser management.
🔗 Connected to: Hooks (hooks/), Page Objects (pageObjects/)

📌 Example: (from DriverFactory.java)

java
Copy
Edit
public class DriverFactory {
    private static WebDriver driver;

    public static WebDriver getDriver() {
        if (driver == null) {
            driver = new ChromeDriver();
        }
        return driver;
    }
}
➡ Ensures singleton instance of WebDriver.

🔹 7. Custom Data Table Type
📍 Location: customType/
📌 Purpose: Converts Cucumber DataTable to domain objects like BillingDetails.
🔗 Connected to: Step Definitions (stepDefinitions/), Domain Objects (domainObjects/)

📌 Example: (from CustomDataTableType.java)

java
Copy
Edit
@DefaultDataTableEntryTransformer
public BillingDetails transform(Map<String, String> entry) {
    return new BillingDetails(
        entry.get("firstName"),
        entry.get("lastName"),
        entry.get("country"),
        entry.get("address_line1"),
        entry.get("city"),
        entry.get("state"),
        entry.get("zipCode"),
        entry.get("emailID")
    );
}
➡ Fixes the "UndefinedDataTableTypeException" error.

🏗 Putting It All Together (Test Flow)
✅ Test Execution Flow (from Cucumber Test Execution)
1️⃣ Cucumber reads the Feature File (guest_order.feature)
2️⃣ Step Definition methods execute (Guest_Place_Order_Steps.java)
3️⃣ Step Definitions call Page Object methods (CheckoutPage.java)
4️⃣ Page Objects interact with Web Elements
5️⃣ Domain Objects store test data (BillingDetails.java)
6️⃣ Driver Factory initializes WebDriver (DriverFactory.java)
7️⃣ Hooks manage setup & teardown (MyHooks.java)

🔥 How a Veteran Automation Tester Would Summarize It to a Novice
💡 "Think of this framework as a well-organized company:

Feature Files (resources/features) = 📝 Business requirements
Step Definitions (stepDefinitions/) = 🏗 Middle managers, mapping business language to Java code
Page Objects (pageObjects/) = 🚀 The workers that interact with the UI
Domain Objects (domainObjects/) = 📦 Data models used across the framework
Hooks (hooks/) = ⚙ Setup & cleanup team
DriverFactory (factory/) = 🚗 Manages browser sessions
Custom Data Type (customType/) = 🔄 Converts test data into Java objects automatically
This structure ensures scalability, maintainability, and reusability in automation testing."